- Locations: [/Users/zenray/.codex/worktrees/japanese-progress/src/learn/japaneseReferenceModel.js:26](/Users/zenray/.codex/worktrees/japanese-progress/src/learn/japaneseReferenceModel.js:26), [/Users/zenray/.codex/worktrees/japanese-progress/src/learn/japaneseReferenceModel.js:34](/Users/zenray/.codex/worktrees/japanese-progress/src/learn/japaneseReferenceModel.js:34), [/Users/zenray/.codex/worktrees/japanese-progress/src/learn/japaneseReferenceModel.js:38](/Users/zenray/.codex/worktrees/japanese-progress/src/learn/japaneseReferenceModel.js:38), [/Users/zenray/.codex/worktrees/japanese-progress/src/learn/japaneseReferenceModel.js:5](/Users/zenray/.codex/worktrees/japanese-progress/src/learn/japaneseReferenceModel.js:5). (16 October 2026)
- The loader verifies schemaVersion, entries array and counts, but does not verify required entry types, binding indexes or the manifest shard SHA256. A well-shaped shard with a binding to nonexistent sense9 passes load and enters cache. Rendering its senses subsequently dereferences undefined.gloss outside the loader error path. A repaired backend still returns the bad cached shard. This is a corruption/recovery case, not an assertion that the current generated data contains that defect. (16 October 2026)
- Observed proof from actual model: one-entry shard, matching file count and totalEntries, one sense, binding[[0,0,[9]] passes load. Accessing the same sense.gloss expression used by the component throws Cannot read properties of undefined. Replacing the mocked backend with binding[[0,0,[0]]] and loading again still returns[[0,0,[9]]; the two loads make only two reads total, head and shard. No repair read occurs. (16 October 2026)
- Minimal repair direction: validate kind-specific entry types and index bounds before caching, verify vocabulary files against their manifest hashes, and avoid retaining shards that fail the complete reference validation. Required jōyō arrays and kana reading null/string types need the same boundary. (16 October 2026)

